Subject: [PATCH 5/7] NDNormalForm: the backward transfer

Checkpoint 7 of the linear normal form's continuation: a stream of records on
which every check passes is a genuine accepting run of N (the decoded virtual
run is N's run under the records' choice bits, halted with output exactly
[true] by the control sweep's pass), and the host-level backward transfer:
the host's backward acceptance lemma with hV gives a first-stopped stream whose
first verdict is acc, which the characterization's first verdict matches.

